{title: 355 - Where Cross the Crowded Ways of Life}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #355 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Ab}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 355}
{meta: category Christian Church - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Ab]Where cross [Eb/Bb]the [Ab]crowded [Cm/G]ways [Db/Ab]of [Eb/Bb]life,
[Fm]where [Eb/Bb]sound [Bbm]the [Eb]cries [Ab]of race [Fm]and [Cm/G]clan,
[Ab]above the [Eb]noise [Ab]of selfish [Bbm/Db]strife,
[Eb/Bb]we [Bbm]hear [Db/Ab]your [Ab]voice, [Bbm/Db]O [Fm/C]Son [Bbm/Db]of [Eb/Bb]Man.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Ab]From tender childhood's [Cm/G]helplessness,
[Fm]from [Eb/Bb]woman's grief, [Ab]man's burdened [Cm/G]toil,
[Ab]from famished [Eb]souls, [Ab]from sorrow's [Bbm/Db]stress,
[Eb/Bb]your [Bbm]heart [Db/Ab]has [Ab]never [Fm/C]known [Bbm/Db]recoil.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Ab]The cup of [Eb/Bb]water [Bbm/F]given [Db/Ab]for [Eb/Bb]you [Ab]still
[Fm]holds [Eb/Bb]the [Bbm]freshness [Ab]of [Cm/G]your grace;
[Ab]yet long these [Eb]multitudes [Ab]to [Bbm/Db]view
[Eb/Bb]the [Bbm]sweet [Db/Ab]compassion [Fm/C]of [Bbm/Db]your [Eb/Bb]face.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Ab]O Master, from [Bbm/F]the [Cm/G]mountainside
[Fm]make [Eb/Bb]haste [Bbm]to [Eb]heal [Ab]these hearts [Fm]of [Cm/G]pain;
[Ab]among these [Eb]restless [Ab]throngs abide;
[Eb/Bb]O [Bbm]tread [Db/Ab]the [Ab]city's [Fm/C]streets [Bbm/Db]again.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[Ab]Till all [Eb/Bb]the [Ab]world [Bbm/F]shall [Cm/G]learn [Db/Ab]your [Eb/Bb]love
[Fm]and [Eb/Bb]follow where [Ab]your feet [Fm]have [Cm/G]trod,
[Ab]till, glorious [Eb]from [G7]your [Ab]heaven above,
[Eb/Bb]shall [Bbm]come [Db/Ab]the [Ab]city [Fm/C]of [Bbm/Db]our [Eb/Bb]God.
{end_of_verse}
